  "steps": [
    "Heat the oven to 400°F.",
    "Whisk the coconut milk, curry paste, garlic and soy sauce (plus the ginger, sesame oil and rice vinegar if using) in a 9x9 in baking dish.",
    "Scatter the bok choy over the sauce, then arrange the frozen dumplings on top in a single layer.",
    "Bake uncovered 20 minutes, until the sauce bubbles, the tops are golden, and a dumpling cut open is steaming hot in the center (165°F).",
    "Top with cilantro, green onions, chili crunch and sesame seeds, and serve."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "The original HealthyGirl Kitchen version bakes covered at 375°F for 15 minutes; Sweet Miscellany bakes covered at 375°F for 30-35 minutes for frozen dumplings.",
    "Frozen dumplings may need a few extra minutes.",
    "Canned coconut cream gives a thicker sauce than coconut milk."
  ],
